<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47991" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέᾱτρον</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέητρον</span></b> , τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεάομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>place for seeing</i>, esp.<i>for dramatic
				representation, theatre</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.67
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1176
			</span></i>, al.; as <i>a place of assembly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.93
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				13.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				976.4
			</span></i> (Samos, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Posidon.
				36
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">J.,
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>19.20</span></i>, etc.;
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. κυνηγετικόν</span>, of the Roman
				<i>amphitheatre</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				43.22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὸ θ. εἰσφέρειν</span> to
			bring upon <i>the stage</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				12.122
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ καλὸν τοῦ θ</span>. a good
			place in the <i>theatre</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>VH</u>
				2.13
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> collective
			for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ θεαταί</span>, <i>the spectators,
				'the house</i>', <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				233
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				194b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				3D.
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκάθηντο θέατρον αὐτῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lib.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					722.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέαμα</span>
			, <i>spectacle</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἐγενήθημεν τῷ κόσμῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>1 Ep.Cor.</u>
					4.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> metaph., of
				<i>life</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τουτὶ τὸ θ. ὑπεκρίθημεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Marc.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
